id: pm-beads-27rw
title: beads validate does not detect dependency cycles
description: "validateBeadsText checked dangling refs, dup ids, unknown status, missing title — but never walked the edge graph, so a circular blocked-by chain (A→B→A) passed validation cleanly. Such a cycle is a deadlock the real bd tooling rejects and produces an unschedulable graph once imported into pm."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-06-05T14:47:46.415Z"
updated_at: "2026-06-05T15:07:33.089Z"
author: codex
acceptance_criteria: validate detects directed cycles in the in-file blocked-by graph (incl. self-deps) and reports them as dependency_cycle errors; only in-file ids considered (no false positives on cross-workspace/dangling edges); acyclic files unaffected; helper unit-tested + e2e verified
resolution: validate now flags circular blocked-by chains (incl. self-deps) as dependency_cycle errors over the in-file graph; cross-workspace/dangling edges excluded so no false positives
expected_result: cyclic beads file fails validation with a clear cycle message; acyclic files pass
actual_result: "verified e2e: 'circular dependency: a → b → a' error + non-zero exit on cyclic file; acyclic passes; 34 tests green"
close_reason: "Shipped in PR #6 (merged): detectDependencyCycles + validate integration"
body: ""
